## 7. Ingestion Algorithm

An upstream packet is accepted only after the verifier:

1. matches its source paths and hashes to the locked repository commit;
2. validates one source-orbit identifier across the four primitives;
3. checks all seven evidence grades and their artifact references;
4. rejects every `PARTIAL`, `CONDITIONAL`, `OPEN` or `NOT_SOURCE` row for
   promotion;
5. rejects any `FAIL` row immediately;
6. validates the `T_fin` commuting square and exact/error certificate;
7. only then instantiates `K`, the corrected Hodge operator and its harmonic
   projector.

The machine-readable schema and current audit packet implement this rule.

